const ST=[,"A child asks why your papers say 'visitor'. Nobody here carries borders.~Explain the gate~She sketches it perfectly from memory and tapes it to the wall.~Say you're lost~A stranger walks you to the science hall and refuses thanks.",
"A saurian elder blocks the path and clicks slowly. It is testing you.~Offer a gift of scent~Rosemary from Home. The elder purrs like a cathedral.~Stand your ground~The elder circles you twice, then steps aside, amused.",
"The ring's traffic AI offers you a free ride to any world.~Take it~You watch nine sunrises in one afternoon and come back dizzy.~Decline politely~The AI logs you as suspiciously polite, and sends flowers.",
"An airship captain offers to fit your gate with a boiler.~Accept the upgrade~The gate whistles now. It also runs 4% faster.~Refuse~The captain sulks, then gives you tea anyway.",
"A frozen clock ticks once. Just once.~Touch it~The ice hums with our own voices, then goes still.~Back away~Something behind the glass exhales.",
"A student hands you a wand and says: point and mean it.~Cast something small~A tiny storm forms above your palm and asks for a name.~Hand it back~The wand sulks, visibly.",
"A deep-folk guide offers to take you below the old skyline.~Dive with them~You drift past drowned libraries where fish read the shelves.~Stay on the raft~They leave you a pearl that hums when storms are near.",
"The Grove asks you a question. The answer takes a season.~Wait for it~Days later, roots draw your name in the soil, gently.~Leave a seed~The Council mutters that seeds are a kind of poetry.",
"You stand in the living ring: fire on one horizon, ice on the other.~Walk toward the fire~Your shadow burns off the ground before you turn back.~Walk toward the ice~Frost writes your breath into the air, and keeps it.",
"A drone hovers and speaks in your own voice: 'Stay.'~Answer it~It repeats your answer one word at a time, learning.~Run~Every screen in the city turns to follow you.",
"A vendor offers one hour of daylight for your torch.~Trade~For sixty minutes the world has colours you had forgotten.~Keep the torch~The crowd goes quiet and pretends not to look.",
"A senator invites you to debate the ethics of the gate.~Argue for it~You lose brilliantly, and get a standing ovation.~Argue against it~You win, and are asked to run for consul.",
"A librarian says you may read one scroll, but only one.~Choose the oldest~It reads: the code for the reversed gate is 2891.~Choose the newest~It is your own handwriting, dated next week.",
"Priests ask you to stand where the solstice light lands.~Stand in the light~For one heartbeat you see every Earth at once.~Watch from the shade~The priest smiles: wise. Most people cry.",
"The city turns toward you as one, without a sound.~Reach out~Something understands you. It cannot be unlearned.~Look away~Understanding waits, patiently, for next time.",
"A polite officer asks whether you are, in fact, a spy.~Say yes~He writes it down and offers biscuits.~Say no~He writes it down and offers a longer form.",
"A court musician invites you to join an evening raga.~Play the tabla~Your mistakes become innovation, and the court applauds.~Just listen~The raga lasts until dawn and you forget your own name.",
"You hear yourself say goodbye before you have said hello.~Say hello anyway~The goodbye rewrites itself to match. Barely.~Stay silent~The hello arrives yesterday, and is very confused.",
"A broker offers you a year of life for a day of your childhood.~Refuse~Your wrist keeps counting. So does his. On his arm you notice 4417.~Sell a minute~He pays in coins that tick.",
"A woman offers you a seat and a bowl. It costs nothing.~Sit and eat~It is the best meal of your life. Quietly she tells you: 2891.~Keep moving~A child runs after you, still holding the bowl.",
"A banner unrolls in the square. Every face on it is yours.~Tear it down~Alarms begin. Nobody is surprised.~Salute~A voice thanks you for your loyalty. You feel it hook in.",
"Two lovers ask you to settle which moon is theirs.~Pick the bright one~They cheer, then argue louder.~Pick neither~They embrace, having won.",
"A robot asks what you want. Anything at all.~Ask for a job~It laughs kindly and hands you a garden.~Ask for nothing~It looks worried, and brings soup."];
