ST[31]="A hatchling lands on your pack and will not leave.~Feed it~It breathes a warm spark and calls you family.~Shoo it away~Its mother's shadow crosses the sun. You hurry.";
ST[32]="A standing figure offers you a chair at its table.~Sit~It pours tea for four. Only three of you are alive.~Decline~It nods, and keeps the chair warm for next time.";
ST[33]="A courtier asks for a favour, to be repaid later.~Agree~It smiles. You will not notice the bill until it is due.~Refuse~The room gets quieter. Every flower turns to watch you leave.";
ST[34]="A voice from below offers to carry your pack down the stairs.~Accept~It is lighter, and so are you.~Refuse~The stairs are patient. They add another step.";
ST[35]="A boot the size of a house stops over you.~Stay still~It steps over, apologising in a tremor.~Run~You become a story told to giant children.";
ST[36]="A shard rings as you pass, and the ring has your name in it.~Hum back~The chord settles into your chest like a second heartbeat.~Cover your ears~The shard sulks, and falls silent.";
ST[37]="Your lamp gutters. The shadows lean in.~Shield the flame~They retreat, hissing, from a light the size of a coin.~Put it out~The dark is gentle for one second, then it is not.";
ST[38]="A storm priest offers a place by the fire in the eye.~Join the circle~Lightning is read aloud like scripture. You are mentioned.~Walk the rim~The wind lifts you a metre and sets you down, politely.";
ST[39]="The water is perfectly still, and something under it is not.~Wave~The surface waves back, a moment late.~Step away~The tide follows, one inch at a time.";
ST[40]="A fallen soldier hands you a sword made of dawn.~Take it~It is warm, and heavier than any blade should be.~Return it~He bows, and returns to the war.";
